; rungs/respond-offence.eval - ONE offence sample for the responsiveness check.
;
; SHARED BY BOTH ARMS OF EVERY OFFENCE PAIR, and that sharing is the point: the
; encounter has to be identical or the difference between two arms is not the
; knob. Each arm applies its knob in respond.eval and then sweeps THIS, so there
; is no second copy of the encounter to drift.
;
; `heal` rather than `reset`, because a reset would also wipe the stat and skill
; the arm just seeded. It restores health/stamina/mana and the hand cooldowns and
; leaves everything else alone.
;
; FROZEN, and a target nothing can kill. The monster is a 1100 hp punchbag
; (skel_warrior 22 hp x50) that never acts, which buys three things: `dealt`
; cannot be capped by the target dying, `taken` stays 0 so no sample can wipe the
; party and end the run, and the number measured is the party's offence alone.
; The first version of this used a 220 hp target, it sometimes died, and the arms
; converged because both were measuring the monster instead of the party.

heal
arena open 9 9
freeze on
spawn skel_warrior 14 11 south 50
tp 14 12
tally reset
step 20
tally
